  "result": "Perfect! I've successfully added payment terms to the invoicing system. Here's what was implemented:\n\n## Changes\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2013 Added new error code:\n- TERMS_INVALID for unknown payment terms\n\n**src/invoices.js** \u2013 Enhanced invoice creation:\n- Added `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)` helper that calculates due dates:\n  - **NET14**: adds 14 days to issue date\n  - **NET30**: adds 30 days to issue date (default)\n  - **EOM**: sets due date to the last day of the issue month\n- Updated `createInvoice()` to accept optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n- Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on all new invoices\n- Validates terms and returns TERMS_INVALID error for unknown values\n\n**test/invoices.test.js** \u2013 Added 11 comprehensive tests:\n- Default NET30 behavior\n- NET14 due date calculation\n- EOM calculations for various months\n- Leap year/non-leap year February handling\n- Month boundary crossing (NET14, NET30)\n- Invalid/unknown terms rejection\n\n**Test Results**: All 164 tests pass (153 existing + 11 new)",
